{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Keypoint Detection & Pose Estimation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Gaussian heatmap target"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gaussian_heatmap(size, cx, cy, sigma=2.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.arange(size), np.arange(size), indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.exp(-((xx - cx) ** 2 + (yy - cy) ** 2) / (2 * sigma ** 2)).astype(np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "hm = gaussian_heatmap(64, 32, 32, sigma=2.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"peak: {hm.max():.3f} at ({hm.argmax() % 64}, {hm.argmax() // 64})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Per-keypoint heatmaps stacked along a channel axis give the full target tensor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Tiny keypoint head"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A U-Net-style model that outputs K heatmap channels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyKeypointNet(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_keypoints=4, base=16):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.down1 = nn.Sequential(nn.Conv2d(3, base, 3, 2, 1), nn.ReLU(inplace=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.down2 = nn.Sequential(nn.Conv2d(base, base * 2, 3, 2, 1), nn.ReLU(inplace=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mid = nn.Sequential(nn.Conv2d(base * 2, base * 2, 3, 1, 1), nn.ReLU(inplace=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.up1 = nn.ConvTranspose2d(base * 2, base, 2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.up2 = nn.ConvTranspose2d(base, num_keypoints, 2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h1 = self.down1(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h2 = self.down2(h1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h3 = self.mid(h2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        u1 = self.up1(h3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.up2(u1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Input `(N, 3, H, W)`, output `(N, K, H, W)`. Loss is per-pixel MSE against Gaussian targets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Inference \u2014 extract keypoint coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def heatmap_to_coords(heatmaps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    heatmaps: (N, K, H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns:  (N, K, 2) float coordinates in image pixels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    N, K, H, W = heatmaps.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hm = heatmaps.reshape(N, K, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    idx = hm.argmax(dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ys = (idx // W).float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    xs = (idx % W).float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.stack([xs, ys], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "coords = heatmap_to_coords(torch.randn(2, 4, 32, 32))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"coords: {coords.shape}\")  # (2, 4, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One line at inference. For sub-pixel refinement, interpolate around the argmax."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Synthetic keypoint dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Simple: draw four points on a white canvas and learn to predict them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_synthetic_sample(size=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img = np.ones((3, size, size), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    kps = rng.integers(8, size - 8, size=(4, 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for cx, cy in kps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        img[:, cy - 2:cy + 2, cx - 2:cx + 2] = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hms = np.stack([gaussian_heatmap(size, cx, cy) for cx, cy in kps])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return img, hms, kps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Easy enough for a tiny model to learn in a minute."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Training"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = TinyKeypointNet(num_keypoints=4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=3e-3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch = [make_synthetic_sample() for _ in range(16)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    imgs = torch.from_numpy(np.stack([b[0] for b in batch]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hms = torch.from_numpy(np.stack([b[1] for b in batch]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = model(imgs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # Upsample pred to full resolution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = F.interpolate(pred, size=hms.shape[-2:], mode=\"bilinear\", align_corners=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = F.mse_loss(pred, hms)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); opt.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Train the tiny keypoint model on the synthetic 4-point dataset. Report mean L2 error between predicted and true keypoints after 200 steps.\n2. **(Medium)** Add sub-pixel refinement: given the argmax position, fit a 1D parabola along x and y from the neighbouring pixels. Report the accuracy gain vs integer argmax.\n3. **(Hard)** Build a 2-person synthetic dataset where each image shows two instances of the 4-keypoint pattern. Train a bottom-up pipeline with PAFs that predict which keypoint belongs to which instance, and evaluate OKS."
      ]
    }
